g","Toegankelijk voor voetgangers met hulpmiddelen","Aangepast toilet"]}},"recurring":[],"targets":{"list":[],"translations":{}},"educational_targets":{"list":[],"translations":{}},"tags":[]},{"id":5700000220,"date_start":"2024-09-14","date_end":"2025-02-24","date_next":"2024-12-14","accept_article27":false,"accept_cultuurbon":false,"accept_paspartoe":false,"is_closed_on_public_holidays":false,"is_closed_on_school_holidays":false,"is_only_by_appointment":false,"is_permanent":false,"is_free":false,"is_pay_as_you_can":false,"is_online":false,"is_canceled":false,"is_soldout":false,"last_updated_at":"2024-12-10T01:01:22+01:00","published_at":"2024-09-09T08:43:22+02:00","publication_state":"published","date_embargo":"2024-09-07","show_in_agenda":true,"is_outside":false,"is_high_capacity":false,"is_not_major_event":false,"backoffice_id":305988,"facebook_link":null,"import_origin":null,"is_part_of":null,"sub_type":"expo","ranking":0.23017706561202741,"languages":{"spoken":["fr","nl"],"subtitles":[]},"categories":{"main":{"id":23,"translations":{"de":"Ausstellung","pt":null,"en":"Exhibitions","it":"Esposizioni","cn":null,"fr":"Expositions","sp":"Exhibici\u00f3n","nl":"Tentoonstellingen"}},"others":{"list":[48,36],"translations":{"de":["Architektur","Museen & Kunstzentren"],"pt":[null,null],"en":["Architecture ","Museums and art centers"],"it":["Architettura","Musei e centri artistici"],"cn":[null,null],"fr":["Architecture","Mus\u00e9es et art centers"],"sp":["Arquitectura","Museos y centros de arte"],"nl":["Architectuur","Musea en kunstcentra"]}}},"translations":{"de":{"name":"Jean Delhaye, architect[e]","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","email":"info@lab-an.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700000220"},"pt":{"name":"Jean Delhaye, architect[e]","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","email":"info@lab-an.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700000220"},"en":{"name":"Jean Delhaye, architect[e]","shortdescr":"At LAB\u2022AN, discover the story of Jean Delhaye, a modernist architect and fervent supporter of Victor Horta. His work reflects the concerns of a time when Brussels, in the midst of a property crisis, was struggling with its urban development on the one hand, and rediscovering its Art Nouveau heritage on the other, after decades of indiscriminate destruction.","longdescr":"Jean Delhaye (1908-1993) is still little known to the general public, but although his name is associated with the \u2018defender of Horta\u2019, he was first and foremost an architect.\n\nAfter graduating from the Acad\u00e9mie des Beaux-Arts in Brussels in 1933 with a degree in architecture and drawing, Jean Delhaye worked in Victor Horta's technical office. At the same time, he developed his own architectural practice, specialising in the construction of modern flat blocks from 1937 onwards, and working on some of Horta's buildings from the 1960s onwards. His work reflected the concerns of a time when Brussels, in the midst of a property crisis, was struggling with its urban development and rediscovering its Art Nouveau heritage after decades of indiscriminate destruction. Delhaye's radical positions and certain decisions, which have since been criticised, were those of a pragmatic man. \n\nFrom the 1960s onwards, and for a long period of his career, he led a veritable \u2018crusade\u2019 to defend Victor Horta's work against his detractors, who saw these buildings as nothing more than \u2018folkloric interest\u2019 and denigrated the \u2018noodle style\u2019, a term long associated with Art Nouveau. Delhaye put his heart and soul into his work, stirring up public opinion, contacting politicians, looking for funding, making inventories, writing, photographing, buying and convincing. He sometimes failed, became angry, despaired, but never gave up.\n\nA tireless campaigner, Delhaye today occupies a unique place among the defenders of Victor Horta's work. He helped to save buildings of inestimable historical value which, 40 years later, are now being restored with the scientific rigour they deserve. These include the furniture from the Wolfers Fr\u00e8res shop and the winter garden from the H\u00f4tel Cousin, now in the Mus\u00e9e d'Art et d'Histoire, the stones from the fa\u00e7ade of the H\u00f4tel Aubecq and the photographic record of the dismantling of the Maison du Peuple.\n\nIn 1937, Jean Delhaye's parents bought the corner building annexed to the H\u00f4tel van Eetvelde. Twenty years later, in 1958, Delhaye began work to install his office and live there with his family. He lived there until 1977. This building, acquired by the Brussels-Capital Region in 2022, is none other than the one that now houses LAB\u00b7AN. The Jean Delhaye, architect[e] exhibition, designed by ARCHistory in collaboration with the Commune of Ganshoren and with the support of urban.brussels and the Service de la Culture fran\u00e7aise, will be on show there from September 2024.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","email":"info@lab-an.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700000220"},"it":{"name":"Jean Delhaye, architect[e]","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","email":"info@lab-an.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700000220"},"cn":{"name":"Jean Delhaye, architect[e]","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","email":"info@lab-an.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700000220"},"fr":{"name":"Jean Delhaye, architect[e]","shortdescr":"Au LAB\u2022AN, d\u00e9couvrez la figure de Jean Delhaye, \u00e0 la fois architecte moderniste et fervent d\u00e9fenseur de Victor Horta. Ses r\u00e9alisations sont le reflet des pr\u00e9occupations d\u2019une \u00e9poque o\u00f9 Bruxelles, en pleine crise immobili\u00e8re, se d\u00e9bat avec son d\u00e9veloppement urbanistique d'une part et red\u00e9couvre son patrimoine Art nouveau apr\u00e8s des d\u00e9cennies de saccages aveugles d'autre part.","longdescr":"Encore peu connu du grand public, si le nom de Jean Delhaye (1908-1993) r\u00e9sonne avec celui de \u00ab d\u00e9fenseur d\u2019Horta \u00bb, il est d\u2019abord un architecte.\n\nDipl\u00f4m\u00e9 en 1933 de l\u2019Acad\u00e9mie des Beaux-Arts de Bruxelles, apr\u00e8s avoir suivi les cours d\u2019architecture et de dessin, Jean Delhaye est attach\u00e9 au bureau technique de Victor Horta. Il d\u00e9veloppe parall\u00e8lement sa propre activit\u00e9 d\u2019architecte, en se sp\u00e9cialisant d\u00e8s 1937 dans la construction d\u2019immeubles \u00e0 appartements modernes, puis en intervenant sur certains b\u00e2timents de Horta \u00e0 partir des ann\u00e9es 1960. Ses r\u00e9alisations sont le reflet des pr\u00e9occupations d\u2019une \u00e9poque o\u00f9 Bruxelles, en pleine crise immobili\u00e8re, se d\u00e9bat avec son d\u00e9veloppement urbanistique et red\u00e9couvre son patrimoine Art nouveau apr\u00e8s des d\u00e9cennies de saccages aveugles. Les positions radicales de Delhaye et certaines d\u00e9cisions, critiqu\u00e9es depuis, sont celles d\u2019un homme pragmatique. \n\n\u00c0 partir des ann\u00e9es 1960 et durant une longue p\u00e9riode de sa carri\u00e8re, il m\u00e8ne une v\u00e9ritable \u00ab croisade \u00bb pour d\u00e9fendre l\u2019\u0153uvre de Victor Horta contre ses d\u00e9tracteurs qui ne voient dans ces b\u00e2timents qu\u2019un \u00ab int\u00e9r\u00eat folklorique \u00bb, et d\u00e9nigrent le \u00ab style nouille \u00bb, qualificatif longtemps associ\u00e9 \u00e0 l\u2019Art nouveau. Delhaye s\u2019investit corps et \u00e2me, agite l\u2019opinion, contacte le monde politique, cherche des financements, inventorie, \u00e9crit, photographie, ach\u00e8te, convainc. Il \u00e9choue parfois, s\u2019insurge, se d\u00e9sesp\u00e8re, sans jamais renoncer.\n\nInfatigable militant, Delhaye occupe aujourd\u2019hui une place unique parmi les d\u00e9fenseurs de l\u2019\u0153uvre de Victor Horta. Il a permis de sauver des \u00e9difices d\u2019une valeur historique inestimable qui, 40 ans plus tard, b\u00e9n\u00e9ficient de nouvelles restaurations avec la rigueur scientifique qu\u2019ils m\u00e9ritent. Parmi eux, le mobilier du magasin Wolfers Fr\u00e8res et le jardin d\u2019hiver de l\u2019h\u00f4tel Cousin, conserv\u00e9s au Mus\u00e9e d\u2019Art et d\u2019Histoire, les pierres de la fa\u00e7ade de l\u2019h\u00f4tel Aubecq et le reportage photographique du d\u00e9mant\u00e8lement de la Maison du Peuple.\n\nEn 1937, les parents de Jean Delhaye ach\u00e8tent le b\u00e2timent d\u2019angle construit en annexe \u00e0 l\u2019h\u00f4tel van Eetvelde. Vingt ans plus tard, en 1958, Delhaye entreprend des travaux pour y installer son bureau et y vivre en famille. Il y reste domicili\u00e9 jusqu\u2019en 1977. Ce b\u00e2timent, acquis par la R\u00e9gion de Bruxelles-Capitale en 2022, n\u2019est autre que celui qui accueille aujourd\u2019hui le LAB\u00b7AN. L\u2019exposition Jean Delhaye, architect[e], con\u00e7ue par ARCHistory en collaboration avec la Commune de Ganshoren et avec le soutien d\u2019urban.brussels et du Service de la Culture fran\u00e7aise, y est pr\u00e9sent\u00e9e \u00e0 partir du mois de septembre 2024.","performers":"LAB\u2022AN x Hotel Van Eetvelde\nCommune de | Gemeente Ganshoren\nService de la Culture fran\u00e7aise | Dienst Nederlandse Cultuur\n\nAvec le soutien de | Met de steun van : urban.brussels\nRecherches, conception | Onderzoek, ontwerp : ARCHistory\nDesign : Dominique Hamb\u00ffe\n\nAVB-SAB\nCIVA Collections Brussels\nC. Delhaye\nHortamuseum\nKIK-IRPA","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","email":"info@lab-an.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700000220"},"sp":{"name":"Jean Delhaye, architect[e]","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","email":"info@lab-an.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700000220"},"nl":{"name":"Jean Delhaye, architect[e]","shortdescr":"Ontdek in LAB\u2022AN het verhaal van Jean Delhaye, een modernistische architect en fervent aanhanger van Victor Horta. Zijn werk weerspiegelt de bezorgdheid van een tijdperk waarin Brussel, midden in een vastgoedcrisis, enerzijds worstelde met zijn stedelijke ontwikkeling en anderzijds zijn art nouveau-erfgoed herontdekte, na decennia van lukrake vernielingen.","longdescr":"Jean Delhaye (1908-1993) is nog steeds niet erg bekend bij het grote publiek, maar hoewel zijn naam wordt gelinkt aan de \u201cverdediger van Horta\u201d, was hij vooral architect.\n\nNadat hij in 1933 afstudeerde aan de Acad\u00e9mie des Beaux-Arts in Brussel met een diploma in architectuur en tekenen, werkte Jean Delhaye in het technisch bureau van Victor Horta. Tegelijkertijd ontwikkelde hij zijn eigen architectenpraktijk. Vanaf 1937 specialiseerde hij zich in de bouw van moderne flatgebouwen en vanaf de jaren 1960 werkte hij mee aan enkele gebouwen van Horta. Zijn werk weerspiegelde de bezorgdheid van een tijd waarin Brussel, midden in een vastgoedcrisis, worstelde met zijn stedelijke ontwikkeling en zijn art nouveau-erfgoed herontdekte na decennia van lukrake vernieling. Delhaye's radicale standpunten en bepaalde beslissingen, die sindsdien bekritiseerd zijn, waren die van een pragmatisch man. \n\nVanaf de jaren 1960, en gedurende een lange periode van zijn carri\u00e8re, leidde hij een ware \u201ckruistocht\u201d om het werk van Victor Horta te verdedigen tegen zijn tegenstanders, die deze gebouwen zagen als niets meer dan \u201cfolkloristische interesse\u201d en de \u201cnoedelstijl\u201d, een term die lang geassocieerd werd met Art Nouveau, denigreerden. Delhaye zette zich met hart en ziel in voor zijn werk, hij wakkerde de publieke opinie aan, nam contact op met politici, zocht financiering, maakte inventarissen, schreef, fotografeerde, kocht en overtuigde. Hij faalde soms, werd boos, wanhoopte, maar gaf nooit op.\n\nAls onvermoeibare activist neemt Delhaye vandaag de dag een unieke plaats in onder de verdedigers van het werk van Victor Horta. Hij hielp gebouwen van onschatbare historische waarde te redden die nu, 40 jaar later, worden gerestaureerd met de wetenschappelijke nauwkeurigheid die ze verdienen. Het gaat onder meer om het meubilair van de winkel Wolfers Fr\u00e8res en de wintertuin van het Cousin Huis, die bewaard worden in de Museum Kunst en Geschiedenis, de stenen van de gevel van het Hotel Aubecq en de fotografische registratie van de ontmanteling van het Volkshuis. \n\nIn 1937 kochten de ouders van Jean Delhaye het hoekpand dat bij het Hotel van Eetvelde hoorde. Twintig jaar later, in 1958, begon Delhaye met de inrichting van zijn kantoor en ging hij er wonen met zijn gezin. Hij woonde er tot 1977. Dit gebouw, dat in 2022 werd aangekocht door het Brussels Hoofdstedelijk Gewest, is het enige gebouw waarin LAB\u00b7AN nu is gehuisvest. De tentoonstelling Jean Delhaye, architect[e], geconcipieerd door ARCHistory in samenwerking met de Gemeente Ganshoren en met de steun van urban.brussels en de Dienst Nederlandse Cultuur, zal er vanaf september 2024 te zien zijn.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","email":"info@lab-an.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700000220"}},"place":{"id":242040,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Van Eetvelde Hotel & LAB\u00b7An","address_street_name":"Avenue Palmerston","address_street_number":"2","address_street_box":null,"email":"team@lab-an.be","website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Avenue Palmerston, 2","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Das Maison van Eetvelde ist ein bemerkenswertes Jugendstilbauwerk aus der Feder von Victor Horta, das 1895-1898 im Auftrag des Diplomaten Edmond Van Eetvelde erbaut wurde. Das Geb\u00e4ude z\u00e4hlt zum UNESCO-Weltkulturerbe.\r\n\r\nDas Geb\u00e4ude wurde 1895 von Edmond Van Eetvelde, seinerzeit Diplomat und Generalsekret\u00e4r im Kongo, in Auftrag gegeben. Sehenswert sind die Eisentr\u00e4ger aus Flacheisen (wie im Industriebereich) statt aus Schmiedeeisen, die Mosaike, der glas\u00fcberdachte Innenhof und die Blumenmotive des Esszimmers.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"pt":{"name":"Van Eetvelde Hotel & LAB\u00b7An","address_street_name":"Avenue Palmerston","address_street_number":"2","address_street_box":null,"email":"team@lab-an.be","website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Avenue Palmerston, 2","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"en":{"name":"Van Eetvelde Hotel & LAB\u00b7An","address_street_name":"Palmerstonlaan","address_street_number":"2","address_street_box":null,"email":"team@lab-an.be","website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussels","address_line1":"Palmerstonlaan, 2","address_line2":"1000 Brussels","description_web":"Created in 2023 to celebrate the 130th anniversary of the birth of Art Nouveau in Brussels, the LAB\u00b7AN (Laboratory Art Nouveau) aims to enhance and promote this unique style and the general and specific themes associated with it. Through its exhibitions and activities, it takes a contemporary look at this Belgian, Brussels and international cultural heritage.\nLAB\u00b7AN is located in the van Eetvelde building, one of Victor Horta's finest creations and a UNESCO World Heritage Site. The opening of LAB\u00b7AN in this extraordinary building makes the Hotel van Eetvelde, a jewel of Brussels Art Nouveau, accessible to the general public 3 days a week.\nThe LAB\u00b7AN x H\u00f4tel van Eetvelde project is managed by the non-profit organisation Patrimoine & Culture, which is also responsible for managing the Halles Saint-G\u00e9ry.\n","description_print":"According to Horta himself, the plans for this house, conceived in 1895, were the most audacious he ever drew. And he did so for a prominent figure, as the client, Baron Edmond van Eetvelde, was the Secretary General of the Independent State of Congo - in reality the unofficial 'Minister of the Congo' - and, therefore, a very close ally of King Leopold II. \n\nThe future owner asked the architect for a house 'for his family', but with as large a living room and dining room as possible, given his frequent social engagements. \n\nThe house is unusual in that it is flanked by two other buildings: a building to the left of it, which was intended to serve both as an extension to the original house and as a rental house and a building to the right of it, a small annex to the main house. ","booking_url":"https:\/\/shop.utick.be\/?pos=LABAN&module=ACTIVITYSERIEDETAILS&s=E4D8C982-7620-86BE-07B4-22D6FF0EFE20&lg=EN","sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"it":{"name":"Van Eetvelde Hotel & LAB\u00b7An","address_street_name":"Avenue Palmerston","address_street_number":"2","address_street_box":null,"email":"team@lab-an.be","website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Avenue Palmerston, 2","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"cn":{"name":"Van Eetvelde Hotel & LAB\u00b7An","address_street_name":"Avenue Palmerston","address_street_number":"2","address_street_box":null,"email":"team@lab-an.be","website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Avenue Palmerston, 2","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"fr":{"name":"Hotel van Eetvelde & LAB\u00b7An","address_street_name":"Avenue Palmerston","address_street_number":"2","address_street_box":null,"email":"team@lab-an.be","website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Avenue Palmerston, 2","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Cr\u00e9\u00e9 en 2023 pour c\u00e9l\u00e9brer le 130e anniversaire de la naissance de l'Art nouveau \u00e0 Bruxelles, le LAB\u00b7AN (Laboratoire Art nouveau) a pour mission de valoriser et de promouvoir ce style unique et les th\u00e8mes g\u00e9n\u00e9raux et sp\u00e9cifiques qui lui sont associ\u00e9s. \u00c0 travers les expositions et activit\u00e9s qu'il propose, il pose un regard contemporain sur cet h\u00e9ritage culturel belge, bruxellois et international. \nLe LAB\u00b7AN est situ\u00e9 au sein du b\u00e2timent van Eetvelde, l\u2019une des plus belles cr\u00e9ations de Victor Horta, class\u00e9e au patrimoine mondial de l\u2019UNESCO. L\u2019ouverture du LAB\u00b7AN dans ce b\u00e2timent extraordinaire rend l\u2019H\u00f4tel van Eetvelde, joyau de l\u2019Art nouveau bruxellois, accessible au grand public 3 jours par semaine.\nLe projet LAB\u00b7AN x H\u00f4tel van Eetvelde est g\u00e9r\u00e9 par l\u2019asbl Patrimoine & Culture, \u00e9galement responsable des Halles Saint-G\u00e9ry.\n","description_print":"28\/10\/24 Selon les dires de Horta lui-m\u00eame, le plan de cette maison, con\u00e7u en 1895, est le plus audacieux qu\u2019il ait dessin\u00e9\u2026 Et c\u2019est encore au profit d\u2019une personnalit\u00e9 qu\u2019il le fait, puisque le commanditaire, le baron Edmond van Eetvelde, est le secr\u00e9taire g\u00e9n\u00e9ral de l\u2019\u00c9tat ind\u00e9pendant du Congo \u2014 dans les faits v\u00e9ritable \u00ab ministre du Congo \u00bb \u2014, et donc un tr\u00e8s proche collaborateur du roi L\u00e9opold II. \n\nLe futur propri\u00e9taire r\u00e9clame \u00e0 l\u2019architecte une maison \u00ab pour sa famille \u00bb, mais comportant, au vu de ses obligations mondaines, un salon et une salle \u00e0 manger aussi grands que possible. \n\nLa maison offre la particularit\u00e9 d\u2019\u00eatre flanqu\u00e9e de deux autres \u00e9difices, de part et d\u2019autre : un immeuble \u00e0 sa gauche, devant \u00e0 la fois servir d\u2019agrandissement \u00e0 la maison initiale et de maison de location ; un b\u00e2timent \u00e0 sa droite, petite annexe \u00e0 l\u2019habitation principale. ","booking_url":"https:\/\/shop.utick.be\/?pos=LABAN&module=ACTIVITYSERIEDETAILS&s=E4D8C982-7620-86BE-07B4-22D6FF0EFE20&lg=FR","sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"sp":{"name":"Van Eetvelde Hotel & LAB\u00b7An","address_street_name":"Avenue Palmerston","address_street_number":"2","address_street_box":null,"email":"team@lab-an.be","website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Avenue Palmerston, 2","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"nl":{"name":"Van Eetveldehotel & LAB\u00b7An","address_street_name":"Palmerstonlaan","address_street_number":"2","address_street_box":null,"email":"team@lab-an.be","website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussel","address_line1":"Palmerstonlaan, 2","address_line2":"1000 Brussel","description_web":"Het LAB\u00b7AN (Laboratorium art nouveau) werd opgericht in 2023 om de 130ste verjaardag van de geboorte van de art nouveau in Brussel te vieren en heeft als doel deze unieke stijl en de algemene en specifieke thema's die ermee verbonden zijn, te valoriseren en te promoten. Door middel van tentoonstellingen en activiteiten biedt het een hedendaagse kijk op dit Belgische, Brusselse en internationale culturele erfgoed.\nLAB\u00b7AN is gevestigd in het van Eetvelde gebouw, een van de mooiste creaties van Victor Horta en UNESCO-werelderfgoed. De opening van LAB\u00b7AN in dit buitengewone gebouw maakt het Hotel van Eetvelde, een juweel van de Brusselse art nouveau, 3 dagen per week toegankelijk voor het grote publiek.\nHet project LAB\u00b7AN x H\u00f4tel van Eetvelde wordt beheerd door de vzw Patrimoine & Culture, die ook verantwoordelijk is voor het beheer van de Halles Saint-G\u00e9ry.\n","description_print":"Volgens Victor Horta zelf was het plan voor dit huis in 1895 het meest gedurfde dat hij ooit had ontworpen. De opdrachtgever was ook niet de eerste de beste: baron Edmond van Eetvelde was de secretaris-generaal van de onafhankelijke staat Congo - de 'minister van Congo', zeg maar - en dus een zeer naaste medewerker van koning Leopold II. \n\nDe toekomstige eigenaar vroeg de architect om een huis \u2018voor zijn gezin,\u2019 maar met een zo groot mogelijke woonkamer en eetkamer met het oog op zijn sociale verplichtingen. \n\nBijzonder is dat het huis in feite een drie-eenheid is. Het wordt geflankeerd door twee andere gebouwen: een gebouw links van het huis, dat zowel als uitbreiding van het oorspronkelijke huis als als huurhuis moest dienen, en een gebouw rechts van het huis, een klein bijgebouw bij het hoofdhuis. ","booking_url":"https:\/\/shop.utick.be\/?pos=LABAN&module=ACTIVITYSERIEDETAILS&s=E4D8C982-7620-86BE-07B4-22D6FF0EFE20&lg=NL","sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null}},"districts":{"list":[9],"translations":{"de":["Europ\u00e4isches Viertel"],"pt":[null],"en":["European Quarter"],"it":["Quartiere europeo"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Quartier europ\u00e9en"],"sp":["Barrio Europeo"],"nl":["Europese wijk"]}},"zones":{"list":[22],"translations":{"de":["Osten"],"pt":[null],"en":["East"],"it":["Est"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Est"],"sp":["Este"],"nl":["Oost"]}},"neca":null,"facebook_id":null,"backoffice_id":4486,"location":{"lat":50.8472189,"lon":4.3803579},"region":"brussels","last_updated_at":"2024-10-28T12:06:41+01:00","published_at":"2013-10-19T01:17:26+02:00","import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"is_in_address_book":true,"is_in_vb_export":true,"resto_ranking":0},"organizer":{"id":247371,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Halles Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_street_name":"Place Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"accueil@hallessaintgery.be","website":"http:\/\/www.hallessaintgery.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 502 44 24","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Place Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Die Halles Saint-G\u00e9ry mit ihrer eklektischen Architektur wurden Ende des 19. Jahrhundert als Markthalle erbaut und spielten in der Br\u00fcsseler Stadtgeschichte eine wichtige Rolle.\r\n\r\nDie Saint-G\u00e9ry-Hallen waren einerseits sowohl legend\u00e4re als auch kaufm\u00e4nnische Wiege der Stadt. Ab dem 11. Jahrhundert stand an dieser Stelle eine dem Heiligen Saint-G\u00e9ry gewidmete Kapelle. Verschiedene Wohnh\u00e4user waren hier entstanden und aufgrund der N\u00e4he zur Senne entwickelten sich zahlreiche Aktivit\u00e4ten.\r\n\r\nIm 16. Jahrhundert erhielt die Kapelle den Status einer Pfarrkirche, die prachtvoll im gotischen Stil erweitert wurde, dann aber im Zuge der Franz\u00f6sische Revolution dem Erdboden gleichgemacht wurde.\r\n\r\nDer ehemalige Markt - und sogar das gesamte Saint-G\u00e9ry-Viertel \u2013 waren ihrerseits in den 1960er-Jahren von der Zerst\u00f6rung bedroht, bis das Viertel in den 1990er-Jahren eine Art zweiten Fr\u00fchling erlebte. Seit 1999 fungieren die Saint-G\u00e9ry-Hallen als Informations- und Ausstellungszentrum rund um die Br\u00fcsseler Stadtgeschichte und das st\u00e4dtische Leben in Br\u00fcssel. An der Bar gibt es Getr\u00e4nke und Speisen.\r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"pt":{"name":"Halles Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_street_name":"Place Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"accueil@hallessaintgery.be","website":"http:\/\/www.hallessaintgery.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 502 44 24","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Place Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"en":{"name":"Halles Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_street_name":"Place Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"accueil@hallessaintgery.be","website":"http:\/\/www.hallessaintgery.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 502 44 24","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussels","address_line1":"Place Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_line2":"1000 Brussels","description_web":"The Saint-G\u00e9ry Market Halls are a fine architectural example of 19th-century public markets in Brussels. The building was completely restored several years ago and is now a permanent information and exhibition space, with urban planning, heritage, and urban renewal as its central themes.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"it":{"name":"Halle di Saint-Gery","address_street_name":"Place Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"accueil@hallessaintgery.be","website":"http:\/\/www.hallessaintgery.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 502 44 24","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Place Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Le Halles Saint-G\u00e9ry (mercato coperto) ospitano un centro d'informazione dedicato al patrimonio e al quadro di vita dei Bruxellesi...\r\nLe Halles Saint-G\u00e9ry (mercato coperto) ospitano un centro d'informazione dedicato al patrimonio e al quadro di vita dei Bruxellesi. Sotto il patrocinio della regione di Bruxelles Capitale.\r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"cn":{"name":"Halles Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_street_name":"Place Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"accueil@hallessaintgery.be","website":"http:\/\/www.hallessaintgery.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 502 44 24","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Place Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"fr":{"name":"Halles Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_street_name":"Place Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"accueil@hallessaintgery.be","website":"http:\/\/www.hallessaintgery.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 502 44 24","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Place Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Remarquable t\u00e9moin de l\u2019architecture des march\u00e9s couverts, les Halles Saint-G\u00e9ry  contribuent \u00e0 valoriser le patrimoine de la R\u00e9gion de Bruxelles-Capitale. Centre d\u2019exposition et de manifestation bas\u00e9 en plein coeur du pentagone, elles ont pour vocation de mettre en valeur les traits de d\u00e9marcation du cadre de vie bruxellois et de son identit\u00e9 urbaine par le biais d'une programmation hybride, allant des expositions, aux conf\u00e9rences, concerts, rencontres et performances \u2026\r\nLe Centre Urbain (guichet d\u2019information r\u00e9gional, pour mieux vous conseiller sur l\u2019habitat durable en R\u00e9gion de Bruxelles-Capitale) est \u00e9galement situ\u00e9 au sein des Halles.\r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"sp":{"name":"Halles Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_street_name":"Place Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"accueil@hallessaintgery.be","website":"http:\/\/www.hallessaintgery.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 502 44 24","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Place Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Verdadero testigo de los mercados cubiertos, las Halles Saint-G\u00e9ry albergan un centro de informaci\u00f3n, bajo la \u00e9gida de la Regio\u00f3n de Bruselas Capital y dedicado al patrimonio...\r\nVerdadero testigo de los mercados cubiertos, las Halles Saint-G\u00e9ry albergan un centro de informaci\u00f3n, bajo la \u00e9gida de la Regio\u00f3n de Bruselas Capital y dedicado al patrimonio y al marco de vida de los bruselenses.\r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"nl":{"name":"Sint-Gorikshallen","address_street_name":"Sint-Goriksplein","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"accueil@hallessaintgery.be","website":"http:\/\/www.hallessaintgery.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 502 44 24","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussel","address_line1":"Sint-Goriksplein","address_line2":"1000 Brussel","description_web":"De Sint-Gorikshallen zijn een prachtig architecturaal staaltje van openbare markthallen in het 19de-eeuwse Brussel. Het gebouw werd een aantal jaren geleden volledig gerestaureerd en doet tegenwoordig dienst als permanente informatie-, tentoonstellings- en evenementenruimte gewijd aan het erfgoed en de levenswijzen in de hoofdstad. Op amper twee minuten stappen van de Beurs vormen de Sint-Gorikshallen een gezellige plek om te ontspannen en nieuwe dingen te ontdekken, zowel overdag als bij het vallen van de nacht.\r\nDe hallen herbergen ook de Stadswinkel, een vereniging die de inwoners van het Brussels Hoofdstedelijk Gewest  wil informeren over het leefmilieu en een kwaliteitsvolle leefomgeving, huisvesting, stadsrenovatie, stedenbouw en ruimtelijke ordening, en rationeel energiegebruik. ","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null}},"neca":null,"facebook_id":null,"region":"brussels","backoffice_id":9562,"location":{"lat":50.84801328,"lon":4.34683241},"last_updated_at":"2024-05-08T15:56:31+02:00","published_at":"2013-10-19T01:26:22+02:00","is_in_address_book":true,"is_in_vb_export":true,"import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"resto_ranking":0},"media":[{"type":"poster","link":"https:\/\/agendabrussels2.imgix.net\/246252e5a55d24aab1060d48a08e386159470adc.jpg","width":3544,"height":4961,"ratio":0.71,"oEmbed_height":4961,"oEmbed_width":3544,"translations":{"de":{"title":"Jean Delhaye, architect[e]","copyright":"\u00a9 Dominique Hamb\u00ffe"},"pt":{"title":"Jean Delhaye, architect[e]","copyright":"\u00a9 Dominique Hamb\u00ffe"},"en":{"title":"Jean Delhaye, architect[e]","copyright":"\u00a9 Dominique Hamb\u00ffe"},"it":{"title":"Jean Delhaye, architect[e]","copyright":"\u00a9 Dominique Hamb\u00ffe"},"cn":{"title":"Jean Delhaye, architect[e]","copyright":"\u00a9 Dominique Hamb\u00