 en zondag: van 08:00 tot "]},"date_start":"2024-12-02","date_end":"2025-02-02","is_also_by_appointment":false}],"date_exceptions":[],"closing_days":[],"child_events":[],"parent_events":[],"accessibilities":{"list":[261,263],"translations":{"de":["Barrierefreier Parkplatz","Barrierefrei f\u00fcr Fu\u00dfg\u00e4nger mit Gehhilfe"],"pt":[null,null],"en":["Accessible parking","Accessible to pedestrians with mobility aids"],"it":["Parcheggio accessibile","Accessibile ai pedoni con supporti"],"cn":[null,null],"fr":["Parking accessible","Accessible aux pi\u00e9tons appareill\u00e9s"],"sp":["Estacionamiento habilitado","Habilitado para peatones con aud\u00edfonos"],"nl":["Toegankelijke parking","Toegankelijk voor voetgangers met hulpmiddelen"]}},"recurring":[],"targets":{"list":[],"translations":{}},"educational_targets":{"list":[],"translations":{}},"tags":["exterior"]},{"id":50012186,"date_start":"2024-10-11","date_end":"2025-02-16","date_next":"2024-12-13","accept_article27":false,"accept_cultuurbon":false,"accept_paspartoe":false,"is_closed_on_public_holidays":true,"is_closed_on_school_holidays":false,"is_only_by_appointment":false,"is_permanent":false,"is_free":false,"is_pay_as_you_can":false,"is_online":false,"is_canceled":false,"is_soldout":false,"last_updated_at":"2024-12-13T01:02:57+01:00","published_at":"2024-07-31T15:34:23+02:00","publication_state":"public","date_embargo":null,"show_in_agenda":true,"is_outside":false,"is_high_capacity":false,"is_not_major_event":false,"backoffice_id":303513,"facebook_link":null,"import_origin":null,"is_part_of":null,"sub_type":"other","ranking":0.3141642477751198,"languages":{"spoken":["en","nl","fr"],"subtitles":[]},"categories":{"main":{"id":23,"translations":{"de":"Ausstellung","pt":null,"en":"Exhibitions","it":"Esposizioni","cn":null,"fr":"Expositions","sp":"Exhibici\u00f3n","nl":"Tentoonstellingen"}},"others":{"list":[46,36],"translations":{"de":["Multidisziplin\u00e4r","Museen & Kunstzentren"],"pt":[null,null],"en":["Multidisciplinary","Museums and art centers"],"it":["Multidisciplinare","Musei e centri artistici"],"cn":[null,null],"fr":["Pluridisciplinaire","Mus\u00e9es et art centers"],"sp":["Multidisciplinar","Museos y centros de arte"],"nl":["Multidisciplinair","Musea en kunstcentra"]}}},"translations":{"de":{"name":"Drafts : From Rubens to Khnopff.","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/fine-arts-museum.be\/fr\/expositions\/drafts","email":"info@fine-arts-museum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 508 32 11","phone_booking":"+ 32(0)2 508 33 33","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50012186"},"pt":{"name":"Drafts : From Rubens to Khnopff.","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/fine-arts-museum.be\/fr\/expositions\/drafts","email":"info@fine-arts-museum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 508 32 11","phone_booking":"+ 32(0)2 508 33 33","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50012186"},"en":{"name":"Drafts : From Rubens to Khnopff.","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":"How is a work of art created ? This is the question that the Royal Museums of Fine Arts of Belgium seek to answer with an exhibition devoted to sketching. At its heart is the creative gesture, presented here in all its forms.\n\nDiscover a fascinating journey through a hundred artworks, immersing visitors in the intimacy of artistic creation. Step into the studio and try to grasp the very essence of the artwork, from the first idea sketched on a blank sheet, a wooden panel, or a piece of cardboard. This immersive experience promises enriching discoveries, offering a new perspective on the behind-the-scenes of creations by iconic artists such as Rogier van der Weyden, Rembrandt, Rubens, Magritte, and many others.\n\nThe exhibition unfolds across time, from the 15th to the 19th century, with a foray into the 20th century. Each stage holds surprises: admire a sketch on canvas by Jacques Jordaens, a model by Alexander Calder, a watercolor by Anne Bonnet, or an oil painting by Delacroix. Preparatory drawings by Rik Wouters stand alongside Fernand Khnopff's decorative projects for the Stoclet House, while the high-reliefs and statuettes by Constantin Meunier and the plein-air sketches by Gustave Courbet or Ferdinand De Braekeleer will captivate you.\n\nThrough a thematic scenography, discover rare works, sometimes never exhibited before , alongside the famous bustling sketches of Peter Paul Rubens.\n\nThis unique exhibition, built around the exceptional collections of Fine Arts of Belgium, also marks the result of a vast restoration campaign carried out over nearly two years by the Museum's teams. Don't miss this opportunity to delve into the secret world of artistic creation and rediscover masterpieces in a new light.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/fine-arts-museum.be\/en\/exhibitions\/drafts","email":"info@fine-arts-museum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 508 32 11","phone_booking":"+ 32(0)2 508 33 33","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50012186"},"it":{"name":"Drafts : From Rubens to Khnopff.","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/fine-arts-museum.be\/fr\/expositions\/drafts","email":"info@fine-arts-museum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 508 32 11","phone_booking":"+ 32(0)2 508 33 33","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50012186"},"cn":{"name":"Drafts : From Rubens to Khnopff.","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/fine-arts-museum.be\/fr\/expositions\/drafts","email":"info@fine-arts-museum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 508 32 11","phone_booking":"+ 32(0)2 508 33 33","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50012186"},"fr":{"name":"Drafts : From Rubens to Khnopff.","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":"Comment nait une \u0153uvre d\u2019art ? C\u2019est \u00e0 cette question que les Mus\u00e9es royaux des Beaux-Arts de Belgique (MRBAB) tentent de r\u00e9pondre gr\u00e2ce \u00e0 une exposition consacr\u00e9e \u00e0 l\u2019esquisse. \u00c0 la base de celle-ci, le geste cr\u00e9ateur, pr\u00e9sent\u00e9 ici dans tous ses \u00e9tats.\n\nD\u00e9couvrez un parcours fascinant \u00e0 travers une centaine d\u2019\u0153uvres, plongeant le visiteur dans l\u2019intimit\u00e9 de la cr\u00e9ation artistique. Poussez les portes de l\u2019atelier et tentez de saisir l\u2019essence m\u00eame de l\u2019\u0153uvre, de la premi\u00e8re id\u00e9e jet\u00e9e sur une feuille blanche, une planche de bois ou un carton. Cette immersion promet des d\u00e9couvertes enrichissantes, offrant une nouvelle perspective sur les coulisses des cr\u00e9ations d\u2019artistes iconiques tels que Rogier van der Weyden, Rembrandt, Rubens, Magritte et bien d\u2019autres.\n\nL\u2019exposition retrace une vaste p\u00e9riode, du XVe au XIXe si\u00e8cle, avec une incursion notable dans le XXe si\u00e8cle. Chaque \u00e9tape r\u00e9serve des surprises : admirez une esquisse sur toile de Jacques Jordaens, une maquette d\u2019Alexander Calder, une aquarelle d\u2019Anne Bonnet ou encore une huile sur toile de Delacroix. Les dessins pr\u00e9paratoires de Rik Wouters c\u00f4toient les projets d\u00e9coratifs de Fernand Khnopff pour l\u2019h\u00f4tel Stoclet, tandis que les hauts-reliefs et statuettes de Constantin Meunier et les croquis en plein air de Gustave Courbet ou Ferdinand De Braekeleer vous captiveront.\n\n\u00c0 travers une sc\u00e9nographie th\u00e9matique, d\u00e9couvrez des \u0153uvres rares, parfois jamais expos\u00e9es, aux c\u00f4t\u00e9s des c\u00e9l\u00e8bres esquisses foisonnantes de Peter Paul Rubens.\n\nCette exposition unique, construite autour des collections exceptionnelles des Mus\u00e9es royaux des Beaux-Arts de Belgique, marque \u00e9galement l\u2019aboutissement d\u2019une vaste campagne de restauration men\u00e9e pendant pr\u00e8s de deux ans par les \u00e9quipes du Mus\u00e9e. Ne manquez pas cette occasion de plonger dans l\u2019univers secret de la cr\u00e9ation artistique et de red\u00e9couvrir des chefs-d'\u0153uvre sous un nouveau jour.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/fine-arts-museum.be\/fr\/expositions\/drafts","email":"info@fine-arts-museum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 508 32 11","phone_booking":"+ 32(0)2 508 33 33","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50012186"},"sp":{"name":"Drafts : From Rubens to Khnopff.","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/fine-arts-museum.be\/fr\/expositions\/drafts","email":"info@fine-arts-museum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 508 32 11","phone_booking":"+ 32(0)2 508 33 33","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50012186"},"nl":{"name":"Drafts : From Rubens to Khnopff.","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":"Hoe ontstaat een kunstwerk? Dit is de vraag die de Koninklijke Musea voor Schone Kunsten van Belgi\u00eb (KMSKB) proberen te beantwoorden met een tentoonstelling gewijd aan de schets. Aan de basis hiervan ligt het creatieve gebaar, dat hier in al zijn vormen wordt voorgesteld.\n\nOntdek een fascinerende reis door een honderdtal kunstwerken, waarbij de bezoeker wordt ondergedompeld in de intimiteit van de artistieke creatie. Stap binnen in het atelier en probeer de essentie van het kunstwerk te vatten, vanaf het eerste idee op een blanco vel, een houten paneel of een stuk karton. Deze onderdompeling belooft verrijkende ontdekkingen, en biedt een nieuw perspectief op de coulissen van creaties door iconische kunstenaars zoals Rogier van der Weyden, Rembrandt, Rubens, Magritte en vele anderen.\n\nDe tentoonstelling speelt zich af door de tijd, van de 15e tot de 19e eeuw, met een omweg naar de 20e eeuw. We gaan van de ene verrassing naar de andere, van een schets op doek van Jacques Jordaens naar een maquette van Alexander Calder, van een aquarel van Anne Bonnet naar een olieverf op doek van Delacroix. Voorbereidende tekeningen van Rik Wouters kruisen er ontwerpen van Fernand Khnopff voor de decoratie van het Hotel Stoclet, hoog-reli\u00ebfs en beeldjes van de hand van Constantin Meunier en in de open lucht gemaakte schetsen van Gustave Courbet of nog Ferdinand De Braekeleer\u2026\n\nDoor een thematische scenografie ontdekt u zeldzame werken, soms nooit eerder tentoongesteld, naast de beroemde bruisende schetsen van Peter Paul Rubens.\n\nDeze unieke tentoonstelling is opgesteld rond de uitzonderlijke collecties van de Koninklijke Musea voor Schone Kunsten van Belgi\u00eb en vormt het sluitstuk van een grootschalige restauratiecampagne die bijna 2 jaar lang door de teams van het museum werd gevoerd.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/fine-arts-museum.be\/fr\/expositions\/drafts","email":"info@fine-arts-museum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 508 32 11","phone_booking":"+ 32(0)2 508 33 33","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50012186"}},"place":{"id":488,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Mus\u00e9es Royaux des Beaux-Arts de Belgique","address_street_name":"Rue de la R\u00e9gence","address_street_number":"3","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@fine-arts-museum.be","website":"http:\/\/www.fine-arts-museum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 508 32 11","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue de la R\u00e9gence, 3","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Die Mus\u00e9es Royaux des Beaux-Arts de Belgique \u2013 6 Museen, 7 Jahrhunderte der sch\u00f6nen K\u00fcnste, 20 000 Kunstwerke und Kunstgenuss vom Feinsten:\r\n\r\n\u2022\tIm Mus\u00e9e Magritte gibt es die weltweit gr\u00f6\u00dfte Sammlung von Werken des gro\u00dfen belgischen Surrealisten Ren\u00e9 Magritte zu entdecken\r\n\r\n\u2022\tIm Mus\u00e9e Fin-de-Si\u00e8cle erwartet den Besucher mit K\u00fcnstlern wie Khnopff, Spilliaert, Horta, Rodin, Gauguin, Mucha und Bonnard das besondere Fin-de-Si\u00e8cle-Ambiente, das um 1900 in Br\u00fcssel herrschte. Mehr als 30 K\u00fcnstler \u2013 vom Impressionismus \u00fcber den Jugendstil, von den sch\u00f6nen K\u00fcnsten bis zur Oper.\r\n\r\n\u2022\tIm Mus\u00e9e Old Master gibt es Meisterwerke aus der Epoche des 15. Jahrhunderts bis hin zum 18. Jahrhundert zu sehen, unter anderem mit der weltweit gr\u00f6\u00dften Bruegel-Sammlung, verschiedenen Werken von Rubens, van der Weyden und Jordaens. \r\n\r\n\u2022\tDas Mus\u00e9e Modern Art zeigt eine Auswahl von Meisterwerken des 20. Jahrhunderts, darunter Broodthaers, Fabre, David, Panamarenko, Alechinsky.\r\n\r\n\u2022\tDie beiden Kunstatelier-Museen Mus\u00e9e Wiertz und Meunier in Ixelles geben einen faszinierenden Einblick in die Welt dieser beiden K\u00fcnstler.\r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"pt":{"name":"Mus\u00e9es Royaux des Beaux-Arts de Belgique","address_street_name":"Rue de la R\u00e9gence","address_street_number":"3","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@fine-arts-museum.be","website":"http:\/\/www.fine-arts-museum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 508 32 11","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue de la R\u00e9gence, 3","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"en":{"name":"Royal Museums of Fine Arts of Belgium","address_street_name":"rue de la R\u00e9gence","address_street_number":"3","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@fine-arts-museum.be","website":"http:\/\/www.fine-arts-museum.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 508 32 11","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussels","address_line1":"rue de la R\u00e9gence, 3","address_line2":"1000 Brussels","description_web":"T