ry.com","email":"info@huskgalllery.com","phone_contact":"+32 478 52 16 46","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700002726"},"pt":{"name":"Diego Herman - How to see through a Fence","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.huskgallery.com","email":"info@huskgalllery.com","phone_contact":"+32 478 52 16 46","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700002726"},"en":{"name":"Diego Herman - How to see through a Fence","shortdescr":"Husk Gallery is delighted to present the first solo show with Diego Herman (b1994, Brussels). ","longdescr":"Husk Gallery is delighted to present the first solo show with Diego Herman (b1994, Brussels). Fascinated by the importance of limits and boundaries in the way we think about space, the Belgian artist with Mexican roots works with the motif of the fence as a strong symbol of the obstruction to the free movement of bodies. Despite the absence of the human figure, Diego Herman composes socio-political landscapes. His paintings raise consciousness about contemporary issues on displacement, identity and humanity. By painting his recurring motifs, such as barriers and borders, abandoned spaces and wild animals, in an unnatural color palette, his paintings transcend the ordinary and become a face of our society.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.huskgallery.com","email":"info@huskgalllery.com","phone_contact":"+32 478 52 16 46","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700002726"},"it":{"name":"Diego Herman - How to see through a Fence","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.huskgallery.com","email":"info@huskgalllery.com","phone_contact":"+32 478 52 16 46","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700002726"},"cn":{"name":"Diego Herman - How to see through a Fence","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.huskgallery.com","email":"info@huskgalllery.com","phone_contact":"+32 478 52 16 46","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700002726"},"fr":{"name":"Diego Herman - How to see through a Fence","shortdescr":"La Husk Gallery a le plaisir de pr\u00e9senter la premi\u00e8re exposition personnelle de Diego Herman (\u00b01994, Bruxelles). ","longdescr":"La Husk Gallery a le plaisir de pr\u00e9senter la premi\u00e8re exposition personnelle de Diego Herman (\u00b01994, Bruxelles). Fascin\u00e9 par l'importance des fronti\u00e8res et des limites dans la fa\u00e7on dont nous pensons l'espace, l'artiste belge d'origine mexicaine travaille avec le motif de la cl\u00f4ture comme symbole fort de l'obstruction de la libre circulation des corps. Malgr\u00e9 l'absence de figure humaine, Diego Herman compose des paysages sociopolitiques. Ses peintures sensibilisent les gens aux questions contemporaines sur le d\u00e9placement, l'identit\u00e9 et l'humanit\u00e9. En peignant ses motifs r\u00e9currents, tels que les barri\u00e8res et les fronti\u00e8res, les espaces abandonn\u00e9s et les animaux sauvages, dans une palette de couleurs non naturelles, ses peintures transcendent l'ordinaire et deviennent un visage de notre soci\u00e9t\u00e9.\n\n\n","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.huskgallery.com","email":"info@huskgalllery.com","phone_contact":"+32 478 52 16 46","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700002726"},"sp":{"name":"Diego Herman - How to see through a Fence","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.huskgallery.com","email":"info@huskgalllery.com","phone_contact":"+32 478 52 16 46","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700002726"},"nl":{"name":"Diego Herman - How to see through a Fence","shortdescr":"Husk Gallery heeft het genoegen de eerste solotentoonstelling van Diego Herman (\u00b01994, Brussel) te presenteren. ","longdescr":"Husk Gallery heeft het genoegen de eerste solotentoonstelling van Diego Herman (\u00b01994, Brussel) te presenteren. Gefascineerd door het belang van grenzen en limieten in de manier waarop we denken over ruimte, werkt de Belgische kunstenaar van Mexicaanse afkomst met het motief van het hek als een krachtig symbool van de belemmering van de vrije beweging van lichamen. Ondanks de afwezigheid van de menselijke figuur componeert Diego Herman sociaal-politieke landschappen. Zijn schilderijen maken mensen bewust van hedendaagse vragen over ontheemding, identiteit en menselijkheid. Door zijn terugkerende motieven, zoals barri\u00e8res en grenzen, verlaten ruimtes en wilde dieren, in een palet van onnatuurlijke kleuren te schilderen, overstijgen zijn schilderijen het gewone en worden ze een gezicht van onze samenleving.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.huskgallery.com","email":"info@huskgalllery.com","phone_contact":"+32 478 52 16 46","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700002726"}},"place":{"id":273385,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Husk Gallery","address_street_name":"Waterloosesteenweg ","address_street_number":"690","address_street_box":"12","email":"info@huskgallery.com","website":"http:\/\/www.huskgallery.com","phone_contact":"+32 478 52 16 46","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1180","address_city":"Uccle","address_line1":"Waterloosesteenweg , 690 \/ 12","address_line2":"1180 Uccle","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"pt":{"name":"Husk Gallery","address_street_name":"Waterloosesteenweg "